<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chewa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The chewa were professional military regiments in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a>. Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amda-seyon-i">Amda Seyon I</a>, who acceded in 1314, restructured the army around these regiments. They supported his expansion southward across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/awash-river">Awash River</a> and the incorporation of neighbouring Muslim sultanates.</p></div>
